Entity System:
Defines the Entity class
Manages entity creation, destruction, and component assignment
Provides methods to query entities based on components

Component System:
Defines various component classes (e.g., Position, Velocity, Appearance, Stats, etc.)
Each component class encapsulates specific data and behavior
Components are added to entities to define their characteristics and state

World System:
Manages the game world, including the world map and entities
Updates the world state based on game logic and entity interactions
Handles spawning, despawning, and spatial queries

Rendering System:
Responsible for rendering the game world and entities
Queries entities with specific components (e.g., Position, Appearance)
Draws the world map and entities on the screen

Input System:
Handles user input and translates it into game actions
Updates entity components based on user input (e.g., movement, interactions)

AI System:
Implements artificial intelligence behavior for entities
Updates entity components based on AI decision-making (e.g., movement, actions)
Physics System:
Simulates physics interactions between entities
Updates entity positions and velocities based on physics rules
Handles collision detection and resolution

UI System:
Manages the user interface elements (e.g., menus, HUD, tooltips)
Renders UI components and handles user interactions

9. Event System:
Implements an event-driven architecture for communication between systems
Allows systems to subscribe to and publish events
Facilitates decoupled interaction between systems

10. Resource Management System:
Handles loading, caching, and unloading of game resources (e.g., textures, sounds, maps)
Provides efficient access to resources for other systems


